    {
        name: "Reading Practice",
        easy: [
            "Welcome to our hotel. We hope you enjoy your stay. Breakfast is served from 7 to 10 AM in the dining room.",
            "Please have your boarding pass and passport ready. Proceed to gate 23 for boarding. Thank you for flying with us.",
            "Taxis are available outside the main terminal. The ride to downtown takes about 30 minutes. Have a pleasant journey.",
            "Check-in time is 2 PM and check-out is 11 AM. Please leave your key card at the front desk when departing.",
            "The airport shuttle runs every hour. The next departure is at 3:30 PM. Tickets can be purchased at the information desk.",
            "Your room is on the fifth floor. The elevator is down the hall on your right. Enjoy your stay with us.",
            "All passengers must go through security screening. Please remove laptops and liquids from your carry-on bags. Thank you for your cooperation.",
            "The hotel offers free WiFi throughout the building. The password is available at the reception. Enjoy your connectivity.",
            "Emergency exits are located at both ends of each hallway. Please familiarize yourself with the nearest exit to your room.",
            "The museum is open daily from 9 AM to 6 PM. Adult tickets cost $15. Audio guides are available in multiple languages.",
            "Please store your luggage in the overhead compartment or under the seat in front of you. Fasten your seatbelt during takeoff.",
            "Our concierge can help you with restaurant reservations, tour bookings, and transportation arrangements. We're here to assist you.",
            "The swimming pool is open from 6 AM to 10 PM daily. Please shower before entering the pool area.",
            "Currency exchange services are available on the first floor near the main entrance. Rates are posted daily.",
            "Please present this voucher at the restaurant for your complimentary breakfast. Valid for two adults per room."
        ],
        medium: [
            "Before boarding your flight, please ensure you have all necessary travel documents including your passport, visa if required, and boarding pass. Electronic devices must be switched to airplane mode during the flight. We hope you have a comfortable journey with us today.",
            "Our hotel features a variety of amenities for your convenience including a 24-hour fitness center, indoor swimming pool, business center, and complimentary breakfast buffet. Room service is available from 6 AM to midnight. Should you need anything during your stay, please don't hesitate to contact the front desk.",
            "When traveling through customs, you must declare any items that exceed the duty-free allowance. This includes alcohol, tobacco, and goods worth more than the specified limit. Have your customs declaration form filled out before approaching the customs officer. Failure to declare items may result in penalties.",
            "The city offers an excellent public transportation system including buses, metro, and trams. You can purchase a day pass for unlimited travel at any metro station. Maps and schedules are available in English at information booths. Most tourist attractions are easily accessible by public transport.",
            "For your safety and security, do not leave valuables unattended in your hotel room. Please use the in-room safe to store important documents, cash, and jewelry. The hotel cannot be held responsible for items that are not properly secured. If you notice anything suspicious, contact security immediately.",
            "Our guided city tour includes visits to the historic cathedral, the national museum, and the old town square. The tour lasts approximately four hours with a lunch break at a traditional restaurant. Comfortable walking shoes are recommended as there will be considerable walking involved. Tours depart daily at 9 AM from the hotel lobby.",
            "If your flight is delayed or cancelled, please proceed to the airline service desk for assistance with rebooking. You may be entitled to meal vouchers or hotel accommodation depending on the length of the delay and circumstances. Keep all receipts as you may need them for insurance claims or reimbursement.",
            "The hotel restaurant serves international cuisine with a focus on local specialties. Reservations are recommended for dinner, especially on weekends. We accommodate dietary restrictions and allergies with advance notice. Our chef is happy to prepare custom meals to meet your specific needs.",
            "When renting a car abroad, make sure you have an international driving permit if required. Carefully inspect the vehicle before accepting it and note any existing damage on the rental agreement. Familiarize yourself with local traffic laws as they may differ significantly from your home country.",
            "Lost luggage should be reported immediately at the airport baggage claim office before leaving the terminal. You'll need to file a formal report and provide your contact information and flight details. Most airlines have tracking systems and will deliver your bag to your hotel once located. Keep your baggage claim ticket as proof.",
            "Our concierge service can arrange various activities including wine tasting tours, cooking classes, adventure sports, and cultural experiences. We work with trusted local operators to ensure quality and safety. Bookings should be made at least 24 hours in advance, though we try to accommodate last-minute requests when possible.",
            "Airport security procedures require you to remove shoes, belts, and jackets before passing through the scanner. Laptops and tablets must be placed in separate bins. Liquids in containers larger than 100ml are not permitted in carry-on luggage. Please arrive at least two hours before international flights to allow sufficient time.",
            "Travel insurance is highly recommended for international trips. It can cover medical emergencies, trip cancellations, lost luggage, and other unforeseen circumstances. Read the policy carefully to understand what is and isn't covered. Some policies require you to report incidents within 24 hours to be eligible for claims.",
            "The hotel provides a complimentary airport shuttle service for our guests. Reservations must be made at least 24 hours in advance through the front desk. The shuttle operates between 5 AM and 11 PM daily. During peak travel times, we recommend allowing extra time for potential traffic delays.",
            "Jet lag can significantly affect your travel experience. To minimize its effects, try to adjust to the local time zone as quickly as possible. Stay hydrated during your flight, get sunlight exposure at your destination, and avoid heavy meals late in the evening. Light exercise can also help reset your internal clock."
        ],
        hard: [
            "International air travel requires careful preparation and awareness of various regulations and procedures. Passengers should arrive at the airport at least three hours before departure for international flights to allow adequate time for check-in, security screening, and potential delays. Ensure all documentation is in order including passports with at least six months validity, appropriate visas for your destination, and any required health certificates or vaccination records. Familiarize yourself with customs regulations for both departure and arrival countries, particularly regarding restricted items, currency limits, and duty-free allowances to avoid complications at border control.",
            "When selecting hotel accommodation abroad, consider factors beyond just price and location. Research the neighborhood's safety, accessibility to public transportation, and proximity to attractions you plan to visit. Read recent guest reviews carefully, paying attention to comments about cleanliness, noise levels, and staff responsiveness. Verify what amenities are included in the rate versus what incurs additional charges such as breakfast, WiFi, parking, and minibar items. Book directly with the hotel when possible as they often offer better cancellation policies and may provide room upgrades or special perks for direct bookings rather than third-party websites.",
            "Navigating foreign public transportation systems can seem daunting initially, but with some preparation it becomes manageable and economical. Before your trip, download relevant transportation apps for your destination city which often include route planning, real-time schedules, and ticket purchasing options. Familiarize yourself with the system's layout including major transfer points and terminal stations. Purchase multi-day passes if you plan extensive travel as they typically offer significant savings compared to single tickets. Keep small denomination local currency for situations where card payments aren't accepted, and always validate your ticket properly to avoid fines from transit inspectors.",
            "Travel insurance policies vary significantly in coverage and cost, making it essential to carefully evaluate your needs before purchasing. Comprehensive policies typically cover trip cancellation or interruption, medical emergencies including evacuation, lost or delayed baggage, and personal liability. However, exclusions often apply for pre-existing medical conditions, adventure sports, and travel to regions with government-issued warnings. Some credit cards offer complimentary travel insurance when you book trips using the card, but these policies often have limited coverage compared to standalone insurance. Always carry your insurance company's emergency contact information and policy number, and understand the procedures for filing claims including required documentation and reporting deadlines.",
            "Cultural sensitivity and awareness are crucial when traveling internationally to ensure respectful interactions and avoid unintentional offense. Research local customs, religious practices, and social etiquette before visiting a new country. Dress codes can vary significantly, with some cultures expecting modest clothing especially when visiting religious sites or government buildings. Understanding basic greetings and phrases in the local language demonstrates respect and often leads to more positive interactions with residents. Be mindful of photography restrictions, particularly regarding religious ceremonies, military installations, and individuals who may not wish to be photographed. Tipping practices also vary widely across cultures, with some countries considering it customary and generous while others may find it insulting or unnecessary.",
            "Food safety while traveling requires vigilance to avoid foodborne illnesses that could ruin your trip. In developing countries, stick to bottled or purified water and avoid ice cubes unless you're certain they're made from safe water. Choose restaurants that appear clean and busy with local customers, which typically indicates fresh food and proper handling. Be cautious with raw vegetables and fruits unless you can peel them yourself, and ensure meat and seafood are thoroughly cooked. Street food can be safe and delicious if you observe the vendor's practices and choose stalls with high turnover. If you do become ill, stay hydrated with electrolyte solutions and seek medical attention if symptoms persist beyond 24 hours or include high fever or blood in stool.",
            "Budget management during extended travel requires discipline and strategic planning to avoid running out of funds prematurely. Create a realistic daily budget that accounts for accommodation, meals, transportation, attractions, and unexpected expenses, then track your spending carefully using apps or a simple spreadsheet. Utilize cost-saving strategies such as cooking some meals yourself in hostels or vacation rentals, using public transportation instead of taxis, visiting free attractions and museums on discount days, and booking activities directly rather than through hotel concierges who often charge commissions. Carry multiple payment methods including credit cards, debit cards, and some local currency, storing them in different locations to protect against loss or theft. Notify your bank of travel plans to prevent your cards from being blocked due to suspicious foreign transactions.",
            "Dealing with lost or stolen documents abroad requires immediate action to minimize complications and security risks. If your passport is lost or stolen, report it immediately to local police to obtain a report for insurance purposes and to prevent identity theft. Contact your country's embassy or consulate as soon as possible to begin the emergency passport or travel document replacement process, which typically requires the police report, proof of citizenship, passport photos, and applicable fees. Make this process easier by keeping photocopies of important documents stored separately from originals and having digital copies saved in secure cloud storage accessible from any device. Consider enrolling in your government's international traveler registration program which can expedite assistance during emergencies.",
            "Health precautions for international travel begin weeks before departure and continue throughout your journey. Consult a travel medicine specialist or your doctor at least six to eight weeks before traveling to discuss necessary vaccinations, antimalarial medications if applicable, and prescriptions for common travel ailments. Assemble a comprehensive first-aid kit including any prescription medications in their original containers with extra supply in case of delays, over-the-counter remedies for pain, digestive issues, and allergies, plus bandages, antiseptic, and any specific items for your destination's climate or activities. Research medical facilities at your destination and locate quality hospitals or clinics before you need them. If you have chronic health conditions, carry a letter from your doctor explaining your condition and medications, ideally translated into the local language.",
            "Sustainable and responsible tourism practices help preserve destinations for future generations while providing more authentic travel experiences. Choose accommodations and tour operators committed to environmental conservation and community benefit, often certified by recognized sustainability programs. Respect wildlife by maintaining appropriate distances, never feeding animals, and avoiding attractions that exploit animals for entertainment. Reduce your environmental impact by minimizing plastic use through reusable water bottles and bags, choosing walking or public transport over rental cars when feasible, and supporting local businesses and restaurants rather than international chains. Engage respectfully with local communities, learning about their concerns and perspectives, and consider how tourism affects their daily lives and environment beyond just economic benefits.",
            "Communication challenges in foreign countries can be minimized through preparation and resourcefulness. Download offline translation apps and language learning tools before departure, as internet connectivity may be unreliable. Learn essential phrases in the local language including greetings, please, thank you, excuse me, and help, which demonstrates respect and often elicits more patient assistance from locals. Carry a phrasebook or translation cards for more complex situations like medical emergencies or reporting crimes. Use visual aids when possible such as pointing to menu items, showing addresses on maps, or writing down numbers to avoid misunderstandings. Consider downloading offline maps and saving important addresses in the local language and script to show taxi drivers or ask for directions.",
            "Managing jet lag effectively can significantly improve your travel experience, especially for long-haul international flights crossing multiple time zones. Begin adjusting your sleep schedule several days before departure by gradually shifting your bedtime closer to your destination's time zone. During the flight, stay hydrated by drinking plenty of water and avoiding excessive alcohol and caffeine which can disrupt sleep patterns. Set your watch to the destination time zone when you board to mentally prepare for the adjustment. Upon arrival, resist the urge to nap and instead stay active outdoors in natural sunlight which helps reset your circadian rhythm. Maintain regular meal times according to the local schedule even if you're not particularly hungry, as this helps your body adapt more quickly to the new time zone.",
            "Airport security procedures have become increasingly complex and stringent following global security concerns, requiring passengers to understand and comply with various regulations. Familiarize yourself with current restrictions on liquids, gels, and aerosols in carry-on luggage, typically limited to containers of 100 milliliters or less packed in a clear, resealable plastic bag. Electronic devices larger than mobile phones must be removed from bags for separate screening, and some airports require you to power them on to prove functionality. Certain items are prohibited in carry-on luggage but permitted in checked bags, including scissors, tools, and sporting equipment, while other items like flammable materials are banned entirely. Allow extra time during busy travel periods and be prepared to remove shoes, belts, jackets, and jewelry which may trigger metal detectors.",
            "Travel scams targeting tourists exist worldwide, requiring vigilance and common sense to avoid becoming a victim. Be skeptical of overly friendly strangers offering unsolicited help, especially in tourist areas, as they may be setting up distractions for pickpockets or leading you to overpriced shops where they earn commissions. Avoid using unlicensed taxis or accepting rides from individuals approaching you in airports, as legitimate taxis queue at designated stands. Be cautious of anyone claiming you've broken a law or that there's an emergency requiring immediate payment, as officials rarely handle fines in cash on the spot. Research common scams specific to your destination before traveling, trust your instincts if something feels wrong, and don't be embarrassed to walk away from uncomfortable situations even if it seems rude.",
            "Packing efficiently for international travel requires strategic planning to maximize space while ensuring you have everything needed without excess baggage fees. Choose versatile clothing items that can be mixed and matched, work in multiple settings, and are appropriate for your destination's climate and culture. Roll clothes instead of folding them to save space and reduce wrinkles, and use packing cubes to organize items by category or outfit. Wear your bulkiest items like jackets and boots during travel rather than packing them. Check airline baggage restrictions carefully including weight limits, size dimensions, and fees for checked bags and overweight luggage which can be substantial. Pack essential items, medications, valuables, and a change of clothes in your carry-on bag in case checked luggage is delayed or lost."
        ]
    }]
},

